In binary if we want to represent a negative integer, we can simply consider or make an assumption that the most significant bit (MSB) is negative.
Ex- 
Binary : 1001
MSB will be 1 (it is first bit)
LSB will be 1 (It is last bit)

So 2^3 is negative + 2^0 is positive , rest are too positive but they are 0 so nevermind...

ASCII values A=65...Z=90, a=91...z=122 

We can keep 1 as True or False and 0 as vice versa, it all depends on user.... Generally 1 is true and 0 is false...

